+\newrev{All five algorithms use the same simulator admission checks in protected mode. Across nine topology--workload conditions, each policy is evaluated for 540,000 simulator steps and records zero admitted modeled hard violations. The common result demonstrates the role of admission across candidate-selection methods. Policy effectiveness is assessed separately through acceptance and the paired HARP--SAF-H differences in Table~\ref{tab:benchmark_paired_statistics} and HARP--CSPF differences in Table~\ref{tab:cspf_paired_statistics}.}
