-\autoref{fig:pareto_design_space} extends this component analysis to NSFNET and GEANT2. The figure shows that full HARP remains on or near the Pareto frontier when safe acceptance is evaluated jointly with SLA violation, latency, and switching behavior. This is important because a variant may appear competitive on acceptance alone while being dominated once routing quality or action stability is considered. The large-topology results therefore support the same conclusion as the Vietnam ablation: HARP's full design is not only safer than unchecked variants, but also provides a better multi-objective operating point than flat, unmasked, or fixed-penalty alternatives.
