+\subsection{\newrev{Sensitivity to Offered Load and Background Occupancy}}
+\label{subsec:hardware_safe_admission}
+\label{subsec:scalability_path_sensitivity}
+\newrev{The load-sweep protocol evaluates the four protected algorithms at seven offered-intensity multipliers from 0.2 to 1.5 on Vietnam, NSFNET, and GEANT2, using 20 seeds and 3,000 simulator steps per seed and multiplier. At multipliers up to 1.0, the multiplier sets the request-arrival rate. Above 1.0, arrival rate is capped at 1.0 while CPU/RAM demand, requested SID depth, and TTL are scaled. We therefore interpret this protocol as a combined offered-intensity stress test rather than a pure arrival-rate sweep.}
+
+\newrev{At zero background chains, the refreshed run comprises 4,200 seed-level policy trials across three substrates, seven intensities, and ten policy and admission configurations (five policies, protected and unprotected). The main figure presents four protected policies; the table additionally reports CSPF. Figure~\ref{fig:load_sweep} compares four protected policies and Table~\ref{tab:load_sweep_results} reports their safe acceptance at every intensity. No protected trial admitted a modeled hard violation. All 20 seeds at each topology and intensity used the same offered trace, so the reported variation is conditional on that trace.}
+
+\newrev{For the 21 HARP--SAF-H contrasts, the paired percentile-bootstrap intervals use 20,000 resamples. The exact two-sided signed-rank test drops zero differences and assigns average ranks to tied absolute differences. Zero-difference counts, effective sample sizes, and rank-biserial effects are reported from the refreshed paired data; all 21 contrasts remain in the Holm family. Appendix Table~\ref{tab:load_sweep_paired_statistics} reports all contrasts. Appendix Tables~\ref{tab:load_sweep_unprotected}--\ref{tab:load_sweep_unprotected_geant2} report modeled violations with admission disabled in the offered-intensity experiment.}
+
